,"type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:05:56Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:05:56Z","body":"This PR stands as an opposite of what I did in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90726 😅\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515254450/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515259910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515259910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515259910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V69IG","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:08:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:08:48Z","body":"> > Would be nice to see how it compares to old `| 32` trick\r\n> \r\n> I actually tried this first. Unfortunately it does not quite cover the 8 bit range. There's 2 blocks of cased letters in there and to cover them we'd need more ifs. Plus common non cased characters like `.` would not be caught, causing them to go into the binary search path - unless you add even more ifs...\r\n> \r\n> I don't have a benchmark for it but I'd wager the branch mispredictions would make it quite slow.\r\n\r\nWell that's what I wrote, for example for to lower\r\n```\r\nif (ch < 0x00FF) {\r\n\t\treturn ((ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z') || (ch >= 192 && ch <= 222)) ? (ch | 32) : ch;\r\n\t}  // else binary search\r\n``` \r\nYou should cover ascii ranges here (I think) without additional if cost","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515259910/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515263739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515263739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515263739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6-D7","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:10:57Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:10:57Z","body":"> This PR stands as an opposite of what I did in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90726 😅\n\nI don't think that's true, they are doing quite orthogonal things and could both be merged :)\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515263739/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515268873","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515268873","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515268873,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6_UJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:13:45Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:13:45Z","body":"Please keep in mind rapid CI runs on this as well, make sure things compile on your own branch before opening a PR and ensure it compiles locally to avoid taxing the CI too much","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515268873/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515302124","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515302124","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515302124,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7Hbs","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:30:26Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:30:26Z","body":"> You should cover ascii ranges here (I think) without additional if cost\n\nI tested the if based code. Performance is very similar to the one based on dense tables[^1]. I am currently without internet but i will update the PR to use ifs for the ASCII range when that changes :) \n\n[^1]: thinking about it, possibly it's because lower/uppercase letters are often nearby each other leading to fewer branch mispredictions","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515302124/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515303039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515303039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515303039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7Hp_","user":{"login":"Chubercik","id":37378746,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3Mzc4NzQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37378746?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik","html_url":"https://github.com/Chubercik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chubercik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T18:30:55Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T18:30:55Z","body":"> > This PR stands as an opposite of what I did in #90726 😅\r\n> \r\n> I don't think that's true, they are doing quite orthogonal things and could both be merged :)\r\n\r\nOh, only a portion of the table that fits a narrower data type got converted - my bad, at first glance I thought you removed other matchings 😁\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515303039/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515410000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515410000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515410000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7hxQ","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T19:29:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T19:30:19Z","body":"> Since we just realized the tables are using `int` instead of `char32_t` for no reason, I change it to `char32_t` in this PR. This should reduce the binary size and RAM use by about 5kb in 64-bit systems.\r\n\r\n**int** is 4 bytes on x64 on all major compilers, so there is no gain in size here I suspect. But being explicit on the size is a plus, no more ambiguity.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515410000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515593487","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2515593487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2515593487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V8OkP","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T21:32:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T21:32:40Z","body":"> **int** is 4 bytes on x64 on all major compilers, so there is no gain in size here I suspect. But being explicit on the size is a plus, no more ambiguity.\n\nWow... I can't believe I didn't know that. Makes the change less critical (though still good to be specific).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515593487/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517729541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2517729541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2517729541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WEYEF","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-04T15:15:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-04T16:02:33Z","body":"Alright, the PR is ready for review again.\r\n\r\nI did some more tests with different `if` based implementations, but they were all equal in speed to the dense table `LUT` implementation, so for both simplicity and byte use I switched to the current implementation. Thanks again to @kiroxas!\r\n\r\nWe also don't save 5kb; the tables were already in 32 bit mode, though i've kept the change from `int` to `char32_t` to be more explicit; it's just more correct and could potentially help portability of the code. Up to 896 bytes are saved from the removed entries in the caps tables, but I don't think that's an important selling point for the PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2517729541/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624507811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99971#issuecomment-2624507811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99971","id":2624507811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cbs-j","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-30T13:23:39Z","updated_at":"2025-01-30T13:24:11Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90726 was just merged. This is good, because it fixed the tables being outdated, but it also decreased performance of `_find_upper` and `_find_lower` further because the table size increased significantly.\r\n\r\nI have updated the PR accordingly (moving the methods to `char_utils` so they aren't generated by the script, for cleanup)\r\n and re-ran the benchmark.\r\n\r\n![newplot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6690f6bc-f5df-4ef7-bf56-6ca41d8c8ba1)\r\n\r\nCompare this to the old benchmark, and you can see the importance of this PR increased a fair bit:\r\n\r\n![oldplot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3e1f0ea-0a93-4c70-a821-339483d3655c)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2624507811/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]